# Design test for opt_retime_acc.v. Forward moves only for now.
#
# $add cuts are supported, and a register with extra readers is copied for
# feed-forward fanout, but a register in a loop is a different case: the
# leftover copy would keep the original D, and that D sits on the after-path
# of the cut, so rewriting the cut would change the copy's input. The observe
# tap would not keep seeing the original register. That is what this category
# is still waiting on, not the fanout itself.
#
# TODO: leave a leftover copy whose D is independent of the cut, then
# -flop f_acc -cut a_acc -forward becomes a real move.
#
# logger -expect error exits yosys successfully, so it has to come last.
design -reset
read_verilog -icells opt_retime_acc.v
hierarchy -top retime_acc
check -assert
# the two readers that force a leftover copy, on both loops
select -assert-count 2 w:acc %co c:* %i
select -assert-count 2 w:cnt %co c:* %i
logger -expect error "other readers need a copy left behind" 1
opt_retime -flop f_acc -cut a_acc -forward
